  "notes": [
    "No native runtime code or ABI changed. Selected core and CLI checks rerun; not a new full-workspace or performance qualification.",
    "Field traversal is shared by component, behaviour/data and nested-record discovery. The registered Health fixture exercises class/rightmost-mixin/superclass precedence and inherited references; CLI freshness verification regenerates and compares its outputs.",
    "The host phase driver supplies one captured tick to systems and behaviours. Fixed/afterPhysics use the same zero-based interval label, while variable callbacks use the captured completed tick count. Both before/after system ordering and zero/multi-tick frames are compared.",
    "addData validates registration and decodes defaults inside the gameplay guard. A caught rejection rolls back previously staged writes.",
    "Regression probes for all three review findings were observed failing before the fixes. Generated Health schema/codec contents remain unchanged after regeneration because the corrected mixin declarations preserve the original layout."
  ]
